  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * @defgroup BiquadCascadeDF1 Biquad Cascade IIR Filters Using Direct Form I Structure
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * This set of functions implements arbitrary order recursive (IIR) filters.
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The filters are implemented as a cascade of second order Biquad sections.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The functions support Q15, Q31 and floating-point data types.
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Fast version of Q15 and Q31 also supported on CortexM4 and Cortex-M3.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The functions operate on blocks of input and output data and each call to the function
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * processes <code>blockSize</code> samples through the filter.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <code>pSrc</code> points to the array of input data and
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <code>pDst</code> points to the array of output data.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Both arrays contain <code>blockSize</code> values.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Each Biquad stage implements a second order filter using the difference equation:
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *     y[n] = b0 * x[n] + b1 * x[n-1] + b2 * x[n-2] + a1 * y[n-1] + a2 * y[n-2]
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * A Direct Form I algorithm is used with 5 coefficients and 4 state variables per stage.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \image html Biquad.gif "Single Biquad filter stage"
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Coefficients <code>b0, b1 and b2 </code> multiply the input signal <code>x[n]</code> and are ref
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Coefficients <code>a1</code> and <code>a2</code> multiply the output signal <code>y[n]</code> an
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Pay careful attention to the sign of the feedback coefficients.
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Some design tools use the difference equation
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *     y[n] = b0 * x[n] + b1 * x[n-1] + b2 * x[n-2] - a1 * y[n-1] - a2 * y[n-2]
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * In this case the feedback coefficients <code>a1</code> and <code>a2</code> must be negated when 
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Higher order filters are realized as a cascade of second order sections.
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <code>numStages</code> refers to the number of second order stages used.
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * For example, an 8th order filter would be realized with <code>numStages=4</code> second order st
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \image html BiquadCascade.gif "8th order filter using a cascade of Biquad stages"
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * A 9th order filter would be realized with <code>numStages=5</code> second order stages with the 
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The <code>pState</code> points to state variables array.
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Each Biquad stage has 4 state variables <code>x[n-1], x[n-2], y[n-1],</code> and <code>y[n-2]</c
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The state variables are arranged in the <code>pState</code> array as:
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *     {x[n-1], x[n-2], y[n-1], y[n-2]}
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The 4 state variables for stage 1 are first, then the 4 state variables for stage 2, and so on.
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The state array has a total length of <code>4*numStages</code> values.
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed, the coefficients are unto
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par Instance Structure
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data struct
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccFQUOk0.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter.
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Coefficient arrays may be shared among several instances while state variable arrays cannot be s
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 3 supported data types.
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par Init Functions
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs following operations:
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instan
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * numStages, pCoeffs, pState. Also set all of the values in pState to zero.
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed in
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manuall
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Set the values in the state buffer to zeros before static initialization.
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The code below statically initializes each of the 3 different data type filter instance structur
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *     arm_biquad_casd_df1_inst_f32 S1 = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs};
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *     arm_biquad_casd_df1_inst_q15 S2 = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs, postShift};
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *     arm_biquad_casd_df1_inst_q31 S3 = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs, postShift};
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * where <code>numStages</code> is the number of Biquad stages in the filter; <code>pState</code> i
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer; <code>postShift</code> shift to b
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par Fixed-Point Behavior
 114:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Care must be taken when using the Q15 and Q31 versions of the Biquad Cascade filter functions.
 115:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Following issues must be considered:
 116:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * - Scaling of coefficients
 117:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * - Filter gain
 118:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * - Overflow and saturation
 119:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
 120:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
 121:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <b>Scaling of coefficients: </b>
 122:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * Filter coefficients are represented as fractional values and
 123:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * coefficients are restricted to lie in the range <code>[-1 +1)</code>.
 124:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The fixed-point functions have an additional scaling parameter <code>postShift</code>
 125:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * which allow the filter coefficients to exceed the range <code>[+1 -1)</code>.
 126:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * At the output of the filter's accumulator is a shift register which shifts the result by <code>p
 127:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \image html BiquadPostshift.gif "Fixed-point Biquad with shift by postShift bits after accumulat
 128:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * This essentially scales the filter coefficients by <code>2^postShift</code>.
 129:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * For example, to realize the coefficients
 130:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 131:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *    {1.5, -0.8, 1.2, 1.6, -0.9}
 132:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 133:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * set the pCoeffs array to:
 134:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <pre>
 135:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *    {0.75, -0.4, 0.6, 0.8, -0.45}
 136:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * </pre>
 137:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * and set <code>postShift=1</code>
 138:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
 139:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
 140:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <b>Filter gain: </b>
 141:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * The frequency response of a Biquad filter is a function of its coefficients.
 142:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * It is possible for the gain through the filter to exceed 1.0 meaning that the filter increases t
 143:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * This means that an input signal with amplitude < 1.0 may result in an output > 1.0 and these are
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccFQUOk0.s 			page 4


 144:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * To avoid this behavior the filter needs to be scaled down such that its peak gain < 1.0 or the i
 145:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  *
 146:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * \par
 147:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * <b>Overflow and saturation: </b>
 148:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  * For Q15 and Q31 versions, it is described separately as part of the function specific documentat
 149:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_df1_f32.c ****  */
